The menu's look
---------------

The in-game menu is drawn with Dear ImGui (MIT, mh4n/port/app/third_party/imgui, with its Vulkan backend) in the Cinzel font
(Copyright 2020 The Cinzel Project Authors, https://github.com/NDISCOVER/Cinzel, SIL Open Font License 1.1: windows/licenses/Cinzel-OFL.txt,
installed as LICENSES\Cinzel-OFL.txt). The font is embedded in the program, unmodified. The design is that of the menu of my own
MH3U port; the colours are this game's.

The game
--------

The game's code is not part of this program. Each player builds their own code library from their own copy of the game
(mh4n/tools/build_game.py), and it stays with them: it must never be shared or uploaded.

Changes to upstream files
-------------------------

Files of the upstream project changed for the Windows port (each carries a notice of the change):
  mh4n/native/src/gpu/native/native_gpu.cpp        the renderer uses the process's shared Vulkan device when one is set
  mh4n/native/src/services/apt/applet_manager.cpp  the Extrapad applet is created
  mh4n/native/src/applets/CMakeLists.txt           extrapad.cpp is built
New files: mh4n/native/src/applets/extrapad.h and extrapad.cpp (derived from the Mint applet, itself derived from
Azahar), and everything under windows/.
